[00:06.52]Hi, Hannah. What are you up to?
[00:10.53]Hey, Mike. Nothing much. I’m at home.
[00:14.96]I’m watching some TV, but it’s not very good.
[00:19.10]I don’t want to do my homework!
[00:21.63]How about you?
[00:23.70]I’m in town. Shopping.
[00:26.59]I’m looking for a new jacket. Do you like this one? It’s £20.
[00:35.74]Erm. It’s OK. It looks a bit old-fashioned though.
[00:42.36]Which shop are you in?
[00:44.71]Tell me you’re not looking for clothes in that old place in Green Street.
[00:49.68]Hah! Of course I am!
[00:52.52]You know I always like to buy my clothes here.
[00:56.48]But their clothes are all second-hand.
[00:58.94]And that means they’re old-fashioned.
[01:02.01]I like the clothes here – they’re really cool and they’re cheap.
[01:08.08]I’m not rich like you, you know!
[01:11.48]Me? Rich? You’re joking of course. Hahaha.
[01:15.98]Go to Barker’s next to the big chemist’s in Market Street.
[01:21.52]They’ve got a sale on.
[01:23.48]They’re selling everything at 30% off the original price!
[01:28.41]And their stuff’s really nice.
[01:30.79]I’m wearing one of their T-shirts now. Only £9.99!
[01:36.09]Yeah, that’s cool. And 30% off? Brilliant.
[01:42.96]OK, I’m going there now. Oh no!
[01:46.84]Now it’s raining and I haven’t got an umbrella.
[01:52.51]OK, it’s not far. Five minutes and I’m there.
[01:57.74]Moments later.
[01:59.68]OK, here I am in Barker’s.
[02:03.38]The shop’s really crowded. It’s because of the sale, I guess.
[02:09.30]Maybe my mum’s there. She’s doing some shopping at the moment.
[02:14.24]So … anything nice?
[02:16.76]Yeah! Look at this shirt! Only £25! I want it!
[02:26.34]Mike, are you crazy? It’s awful.
[02:30.64]No, it’s not.
[02:32.41]I love wearing bright colours.
[02:35.11]They make me feel happy. It’s perfect for a rainy day.
[02:40.67]I think you’re wasting your money and my time.
[02:45.05]Anyway – are you looking for a jacket or a shirt?
[02:49.09]Oh yes, you’re right. You’re better at clothes than me.
[02:54.83]Come and help me. You’re not doing anything, are you?
[02:58.15]That sounds like a bad idea. It’s raining – remember?
